WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
So my name is Graeme Clark and I'm the director of Ethos Safety.

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.560
So Ethos Safety is a full-service health and safety consultancy based in the Highlands of Scotland.

3
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.640
Previously, we'd used paper templates for inspecting or auditing sites.

4
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:26.080
And that was nothing more complicated than a clipboard and a pre-printed template that you would complete when you went around a site auditing the performance.

5
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.760
We then moved to using cloud-based software.

6
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:40.520
But we spent quite a lot of time focusing on the iPad, looking at the iPad, scrolling up, making these ticks in boxes or physically typing in boxes and taking a photograph for that topic.

7
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:53.360
So the old method would probably take anywhere from 40 to 60 minutes on site, but it did require some degree of administration once you'd left the site.

8
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.520
I think it was deceptively easy.

9
00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:09.280
It felt almost like we weren't putting enough effort in using Quickler because it was deceptively easy to capture the data by purely just describing it or just taking a series, a short series of photographs.

10
00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:22.400
We know that all I need to do is snap a couple of photographs and I do mean snap, you know, physically go click, click, click and then think for three or four sentences and give that to Quickler as a voice note.

11
00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:30.920
And that is so efficient that we're maybe only spending a fifth, if not a sixth of the time actually doing the task.

12
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.680
We spend the rest of the remaining time interacting with people, which is what we're there to do.

13
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.960
We're there to actually change people's behaviours on health and safety.

14
00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:42.120
We're now spending that time speaking directly to people.

15
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:51.720
So looking people in the eye and talking to them, having easier conversations because we're not slavishly following it because we know we've got a tool in our pocket or in our hand.

16
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.640
Which is much smaller because it's a mobile phone.

17
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.320
The beauty with Quickler is we actually can see how long it takes to edit the report.

18
00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.040
There's a metric against that, so time taken to edit.

19
00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.640
It's taken on average between five to 10 minutes.

20
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:14.760
And some of this is actually because we've chosen to leave the activity of adding certain things until we go back to the office.

21
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:23.840
So we're able to top and tail the inspection activity much quicker than we did before.

22
00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.760
So we're moving on to other tasks.

23
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:33.160
So we're almost able to do them completely in exclusion of any other activity and then move straight on to something else.

24
00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.720
So there is no requirement to revisit the task.

25
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.880
So it's a one and done basically.

26
00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.480
We were able to do exactly the same as we did before report wise.

27
00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.960
But we were able to do it quicker and we were able to do it slicker.

28
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:56.400
We had the ability to actually generate a high quality report that needed very minimal admin or tidying up afterwards.

29
00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.400
And we were then able to bounce from that job to the next job.

30
00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:07.680
Initially we were quite terse with it, so we didn't give it a huge amount of information when we were giving a voice note for a particular subject.

31
00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:11.680
Now we're probably adding two or three sentences to that voice notes.

32
00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:20.240
But in reality, with a longer, more explanatory, descriptive voice notes, the result is really much better.

33
00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.280
I wouldn't hesitate to recommend it to anybody else.

34
00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:30.160
Everybody I've ever shown it to almost looks on with a gaze of wonder to say, oh, how is it doing that?

35
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.640
It's a vital part of what we now do day to day.
